From: Anfernee Cao <anferneemelokc5@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: core: clear states after freeing them

genpd_free_data() frees the power states through ->free_states(), but
leaves the states pointer and count referring to the freed allocation.
Clear both fields so later cleanup does not free the states again.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/179259111932.19580.13027750156272888992@gmail.com
Fixes: 9d976d6721df ("cpuidle: Factor-out power domain related code from PSCI domain driver")
Signed-off-by: Anfernee Cao <anferneemelokc5@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/core.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/core.c b/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
index 052ec478dfcc4ced0b2850a6775ea29d464e972a..12db69f53aeea4cacb34145cd40d3d101a30b005 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
@@ -2353,8 +2353,11 @@ static void genpd_free_data(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd)
 		ida_free(&genpd_ida, genpd->device_id);
 	if (genpd_is_cpu_domain(genpd))
 		free_cpumask_var(genpd->cpus);
-	if (genpd->free_states)
+	if (genpd->free_states) {
 		genpd->free_states(genpd->states, genpd->state_count);
+		genpd->states = NULL;
+		genpd->state_count = 0;
+	}
 	kfree(genpd->gd);
 }
 
